-- title:
--   Mod p Galois representation of an elliptic curve has cyclotomic determinant
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb{Q}$ and $p$ a prime. Assume the discriminant satisfies $W.\Delta \neq 0$; that the group of $p$-torsion points of $W$ over $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\,\mathbb{Q}$, i.e. the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule `Submodule.torsionBy ℤ (W⁄(AlgebraicClosure ℚ)).Point p`, has cardinality $p^{2}$; and that the natural action of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ on that $p$-torsion module by $\mathbb{Z}/p$-linear endomorphisms, `galoisRepModuleEnd`, factors through a finite level, i.e. there is an intermediate field $L$ with $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq L \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ finite over $\mathbb{Q}$ such that every $\sigma$ fixing $L$ pointwise acts as the identity. These data give a two-dimensional residual representation over $\mathbb{Z}/p$ with underlying space the $p$-torsion and with this Galois action, and [`GaloisRepAdic.ofResidualGaloisRep`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L196) regards it as a rank-two representation over the local ring $\mathbb{Z}/p$, its adic continuity coming from the factorisation through $L$. The conclusion is the predicate `DetIsCyclotomic` for $p$: first, $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $\mathbb{Z}/p$ (which is zero, and $p = 0$ there); second, for every $n \in \mathbb{N}$, every $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ and every $a \in \mathbb{N}$ such that $\sigma\mu = \mu^{a}$ for all $\mu \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\mu^{p^{n}} = 1$, the difference $\det(\rho(\sigma)) - a$ lies in the ideal of $\mathbb{Z}/p$ generated by $p^{n}$. Since that ideal is all of $\mathbb{Z}/p$ for $n = 0$ and zero for $n \geq 1$, the content is the identity $\det(\rho(\sigma)) = a$ in $\mathbb{Z}/p$ at level one.
--
--   This is the Weil-pairing computation of the determinant of the mod $p$ representation attached to an elliptic curve over $\mathbb{Q}$: the determinant is the mod $p$ cyclotomic character, here expressed in the finite-level form demanded by the local condition `DetIsCyclotomic`. It supplies this conjunct of the local conditions in the downstream analysis of the residual representation, e.g. in the production of a Deligne ordinary shape in the ordinary or multiplicative case and in the arguments about stable lines and good primes.
